     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Nefertiry Meryetmut\", \"choices\": [\"C1\"], \"reasoning\": \"C1 is Nfr.t-jr.j mr.yt-Mw.t, made of nfr.t 'beautiful' + jr.j 'companion' (Nefertari), then mr.yt 'beloved' + Mw.t 'Mut' (Meryetmut). Its TLA spellings are Nefertari-Meryt-Mut and Nefertari. Record 1 reads letter by letter as these words in the same order. 'Nefer-t' gives n-f-r-.t. 'iry' gives j-r-.j, with both j rendered as i and y. 'Mery-et' gives m-r-y-.t. 'mut' gives M-w-.t, with w rendered as u. No consonant is added and none is left out. The words are the same as in the TLA spellings: Nefertari Meryetmut, 'beautiful companion, beloved of Mut'. Nefertiry is only a different vocalisation of Nefertari. C1 is therefore the same name as record 1.\"}"
     }
